                  A Venn diagram for this problem. The circles overlap. The region contained within only one circle, but not both, is shaded.
                </p>
              </description>
            </image>
                </p>
              </li>
            </ol>
        </statement>
        <answer>
          <p>
            (A)
          </p>
        </answer>
      </exercise>

      <exercise number="3"><!-- #3 -->
        <statement>
          <p>
            Which linear programming problem is represented by the initial simplex tableau below?
              <me>
                \begin{array}{rrrrrr|r}
                  x \amp y \amp s_1 \amp s_2 \amp s_3 \amp Z \amp c \\
                  \hline
                  3 \amp 4 \amp 1 \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp 30 \\
                  2 \amp 6 \amp 0 \amp 1 \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp 45 \\
                  0 \amp 4 \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp 1 \amp 0 \amp 24 \\
                  \hline
                  -5 \amp -7 \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp 1 \amp 0
                \end{array}
              </me>
          </p>
            <ol marker="(A)">
              <li>
                <p>
              <md>
                <mrow>\text{Maximize } \amp P = -5x-7y</mrow>
                <mrow>\text{subject to } \amp 3x+4y\leq 30</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp 2x+6y\leq 45</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp 4y\leq 24</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp x\geq 0, y\geq 0</mrow>
              </md>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
              <md>
                <mrow>\text{Maximize } \amp P = 5x+7y</mrow>
                <mrow>\text{subject to } \amp 3x+4y\geq 30</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp 2x+6y\geq 45</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp 4y\geq 24</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp x\leq 0, y\leq 0</mrow>
              </md>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
              <md>
                <mrow>\text{Maximize } \amp c=5x+7y+P</mrow>
                <mrow>\text{subject to } \amp 3x+4y\leq 30</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp 2x+6y\leq 45</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp 4y\leq 24</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp x\geq 0, y\geq 0</mrow>
              </md>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
              <md>
                <mrow>\text{Maximize } \amp P=5x+7y</mrow>
                <mrow>\text{subject to } \amp 3x+4y\leq 30</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp 2x+6y\leq 45</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp 4y\leq 24</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp x\geq 0, y\geq 0</mrow>
              </md>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
              <md>
                <mrow>\text{Maximize } \amp P=7x+5y</mrow>
                <mrow>\text{subject to } \amp 4x+3y\leq 30</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp 6x+2y\leq 45</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp 4y\leq 24</mrow>
                <mrow>\amp x\geq 0, y\geq 0</mrow>
              </md>
                </p>
              </li>
            </ol>
        </statement>
        <answer>
          <p>
            (D)
          </p>
        </answer>
      </exercise>

      <exercise number="4"><!-- #4 -->
        <statement>
          <p>
            Consider the experiment of randomly selecting a distinct letter from the word "reveille" and then drawing a card from a standard deck of <m>52</m> cards and noting the color. Using <m>R</m> to designate a red card is drawn and <m>B</m> for a black card is drawn, which of the following choices below gives the sample space for the experiment?
          </p>
            <ol marker="(A)">
              <li>
                <p>
                  <m>S=\{rR,eR,vR,eR,iR,lR,lR,eR,rB,eB,vB,iB,lB\}</m>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  <m>S=\{rR,eR,vR,iR,lR,rB,eB,vB,iB,lB\}</m>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  <m>S=\{r,e,v,i,l,R,B\}</m>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  <m>S=\{rR,eR,vR,lR,eB,vB,iB,lB\}</m>
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  None of these.
                </p>
              </li>
            </ol>
        </statement>
        <answer>
          <p>
            (B)
          </p>
        </answer>
      </exercise>

      <exercise number="5"><!-- #5 -->
        <statement>
          <p>
            Find the next pivot element in the simplex tableau below.
              <me>
                \begin{array}{rrrrrrr|r}
                  x \amp y \amp z \amp s_1 \amp s_2 \amp s_3 \amp Z \amp c \\
                  \hline
                  1 \amp 2 \amp 4 \amp \dfrac{1}{2} \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp 12 \\
                  0 \amp 5 \amp 10 \amp \dfrac{5}{2} \amp 1 \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp 20 \\
                  0 \amp 0 \amp -6 \amp 4 \amp 0 \amp 1 \amp 0 \amp 5 \\
                  \hline
                  0 \amp -5 \amp -2 \amp \dfrac{7}{2} \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp 1 \amp 0
                \end{array}
              </me>
          </p>
            <ol marker="(A)">
              <li>
                <p>
                  The element in row <m>\#2</m>, column <m>\#2</m>.
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  The element in row <m>\#1</m>, column <m>\#2</m>.
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  The element in row <m>\#3</m>, column <m>\#2</m>.
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  The element in row <m>\#1</m>, column <m>\#3</m>.
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  The element in row <m>\#3</m>, column <m>\#3</m>.
                </p>
              </li>
            </ol>
        </statement>
        <answer>
          <p>
            (A)
          </p>
        </answer>
      </exercise>
    </paragraphs>
  
  </worksheet>

